Discovering that a partner has been unfaithful is one of the most painful experiences that a person can go through. It can shake your sense of trust, security, and even identity. Today we're going to talk with a psychologist who studies infidelity and commitment about why people cheat and what happens to relationships when they do. We'll talk about what the research says about infidelity. Is it increasing in the age of dating apps, social media, and chatbot companions? How does psychologists think about what constitutes? cheating? Does there have to be a physical element? Can relationships recover after one partner cheats? And how do psychologists help individuals and couples navigate what comes next after a betrayal?

2
