He felt as though he was betraying his wife's trust in some way, that it crossed some boundary or expectation or agreement spoken or unspoken that they had between each other. And the fact that, you know, in the way that he said that, it was as if it was a confession, right? And we make confessions like that if we know we've done something that might hurt someone else. Right. Although not usually to Playboy magazine. Excellent point. These days, a lot of people talk about having a work husband or a work wife, right? Somebody at their job with whom they have a really close relationship. Is that a form of cheating? I like that question a lot because it does seem like that is a common phrase we hear these days that indicates some kind of close relationship.

