but met online in some way. And those kinds of relationships certainly can hurt the other person and feel like a betrayal. I think the flip side of that is that technology also means that there are some additional checks and balances in that, right? That if you're trying to hide something that's happening online, it's possible. But there's also more eyes on those relationships, right? It's easier to know where your partner is because of Find My and other apps that, you know, you may share and track one another on. So in some ways, I think that's related to the definition,

