sort of changing and being more about, as you said, if it feels like it, it likely is infidelity. But I do think there are some ways that there is a higher level of monitoring one another that can build both trust in some ways and a sense of concern in some other ways. I want to talk a little bit about why we think people, cheat. I mean, there have to be scores of reasons why people are unfaithful, but what does the research tell us? Is it mostly because of relationship dissatisfaction or boredom or maybe a desire to get back at a partner you're angry at? And are there warning flags that might tell us that someone is highly likely to cheat? I think all of those reasons that you just gave are reasons that

