at my spouse. I just think we sort of create that narrative sometimes to justify the behavior when it was really more happenstance that someone wound up cheating. So the opportunity presented itself and it was just too tantalizing. That's right. Does the reason behind an affair influence whether couples are able to recover and are there some types of betrayals that are harder to move past than others? It not only matters for the depth of the betrayal, but it matters in part for the person who is participating in the affair, the one who is cheating. If they are very strongly connected to this person, it's going to be harder for them to end the affair to close that relationship and to recover from the breakup and the grief that they may feel when that affair ends and then be able to

