predict who's likely to cheat? Are there characteristics or relationship patterns that make infidelity more likely? Not well, but isn't this a thing about psychology? So much of our work is trying to predict human behavior and we explain very little in outcomes in human behavior. I will say one thing that does precede infidelity is an increase in what psychologists, the social psychologists call alternative monitoring, how much someone is looking at the availability of other partners or their awareness of other people who they may have some connection with, have some attraction to. So we do see that there is an increase in that concept of alternative monitoring before infidelity happens. And we do see that there is an increase in that concept of alternative monitoring before infidelity

