happens. And we think of that as a type of commitment. If you're highly dedicated, committed to your partner, you're just less likely to be thinking about and looking around at other people, essentially. So the more, you know, we might see that in ourselves, right? We could do a self-assessment, you know, how much am I kind of just paying attention to how much I like my friend's partner or like this person at work or, huh, that person seems really attractive. You know, how much sort of headspace is that taking up is one tiny predictor of infidelity? What about people who have serial relationships that keep breaking up because the other person cheated? Are there characteristics of those people who are more likely to get involved again with cheaters? It's sort of like people who

