27
00:21:18.000 --> 00:22:22.000
I'm open to the idea that you could learn some good things in those relationships. relationships, perhaps. But I think it comes down to it's going to feel like betrayal to someone else. If you're sharing parts of yourself that we typically think of are really only meant for your partner, it will hurt the other person. Right. And so if you're having an in-depth relationship, whether it has some sexual overtones or not, that kind of relationship, may mean, likely means, I think, that you are missing out on a true connection with your partner and that your partner will likely be hurt by that, that you're sharing parts of yourself that are typically reserved for that primary relationship. And chatbots tend to affirm what you want them to say. I mean, the thing is, maybe you're having some tension with your partner. You go to a chatbot, which will always say, oh, you're all right, you're right.

