00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:54.000
And then the third stage is really about what do we do next to move on? For some couples, that means ending the relationship, but they've done the work to process it well and understand that together, which will make their next relationship experiences better. Or if they're going on to co-parent together, it'll make their new relationship, coparenting relationship better. For many couples, it means not allowing the affair to control their lives and their relationship anymore and really thinking about what do we want for our new relationship? It's going to look different for many different reasons.

32
00:24:54.000 --> 00:25:21.000
We want it to look different. We want to make sure this doesn't happen again. We want to make sure it's fulfilling to both of us. So it gives a couple an opportunity to really redefine their relationship and set new expectations around communication, around talking with other people, all of those components, and really make decisions together, which they may not have done for many years, if ever.

